# React Component Rules

## Component Pattern
- Functional components ONLY — never class components
- Arrow function syntax ONLY
- Define props as TypeScript interface with `Props` suffix

```tsx
interface UserCardProps {
  name: string;
  email: string;
  onEdit?: () => void;
}

const UserCard: React.FC<UserCardProps> = ({ name, email, onEdit }) => {
  return (
    <Box>
      <Typography variant="h6">{name}</Typography>
      <Typography variant="body2">{email}</Typography>
      {onEdit && <Button onClick={onEdit}>Edit</Button>}
    </Box>
  );
};

export default UserCard;
```

## MUI Usage
- Use MUI components for layout: `Box`, `Stack`, `Grid`, `Container`
- Use `Typography` for all text — never raw `<p>`, `<h1>`, etc.
- Use `Button`, `IconButton`, `TextField` for interactive elements
- Apply styles through MUI's `sx` prop or `styled()` — not inline CSS objects
- Use theme tokens: `theme.palette.primary.main`, `theme.spacing(2)`

## File Naming
- File: kebab-case (`user-card.tsx`)
- Component: PascalCase (`UserCard`)
- Directory: kebab-case (`user-card/`)

## Accessibility (Default)
- All `img` elements must have `alt` text
- Interactive elements need `aria-label` when text content is not descriptive
- Use semantic HTML elements within MUI components
- Buttons must be keyboard accessible (MUI handles this by default)

## Exports
- Use default export for the component
- Use named exports for related types/utilities
